Mātali urges Rāma to loose Brahmā's arrow --- Rāma consecrates the unfailing world-fire shaft --- Rāma hurls the arrow into Rāvaṇa's heart --- The arrow returns to Rāma's quiver --- Rāvaṇa falls lifeless like Vr̥tra --- Leaderless rākṣasas flee toward Laṅkā --- Monkeys chase them shouting victory --- Gods sound drums and rain flowers --- Sugrīva and friends honor victorious Rāma
